{
    "title": "Stakeholder Engagement: Investors and Shareholders",
    "summary": "The page outlines stakeholder engagement for investors/shareholders, covering identification as a key stakeholder group (though not vulnerable/marginalized), communication channels (email, SMS, newspaper, pamphlets, advertisement, community meetings, notice board, website, online surveys, focus groups, one-on-one interviews, non-deal roadshows, investor events, reverse roadshows, geo-based management meetings, webinars), frequency of engagement (quarterly), and purpose/scope of engagement. Purpose: maximize shareholder value, attract investment, and provide transparent information. Scope: regular financial reporting, investor conferences, analyst interactions, and timely updates on business performance, strategy, and corporate governance.",
}

{
  "title": "Stakeholder Engagement Channels, Purposes, Scope, and CSR Aspects",
  "summary": "This page presents a matrix of stakeholder engagement channels, identifying whether groups are vulnerable or marginalized, and specifying communication methods and engagement frequency for clients and communities. It details client engagement purposes (exceptional experiences, relationships, expectations) and scope (quality products, personalized solutions, support, feedback, surveys, continuous improvement, resolving challenges, technology feedback, new opportunities, footprint growth, upsell, ABM plans, QBR process). Aspects discussed include contract compliance, resource management, payment queries, and delivery challenges. For CSR initiatives, it outlines purposes (local development, social wellbeing, sustainable practices), scope (community development, early childhood care, education, skill-building, healthcare, WASH, sports, volunteering, disaster risk reduction, assessments, grievance redressal), and aspects discussed (education, WASH, malnutrition, environmental sustainability, skill development, employability).",
}
